{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"The stream experiment was slower and has been disabled. Two local tunings are clearly beneficial: larger elementwise tiles cut the activation pass from about 45 μs to 28 μs at 8192 tokens, and a single fused outer-product kernel replaces both weight-gradient GEMMs for 1–8 tokens (about 9–15 μs instead of 18–20 μs). I’m integrating those paths and rechecking end-to-end latency and accuracy before spending another verifier run."}}
