{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"For the 4–128 token cases, a mixed representation is faster than the BF16 residual scheme: storing the activation gradients directly in FP16 retains enough precision (local match ratios ≥99.96%), halves the corrective GEMM, and saves about 3–4 μs. I’m keeping the more conservative two-term BF16 representation for 1–2 tokens, where it is both faster and exactest."}}
